{{template "top.gohtml" .}}

<h1>Mail app — Configuration</h1>
<p class="note">MailApp.sendEmail hands every message to the bundled send-only
relay on the compose network — host <code>mailer</code>, port 25, no credentials,
nothing to configure beyond the toggle and the sender address. The relay
delivers straight to recipient MX servers; its DNS checklist (PTR, SPF) lives
in the README. MailApp.read is not supported — the relay is send-only.</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/mail" class="card">
  <label><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" {{if .Mail.Enabled}}checked{{end}} /> Enable the mail app</label>

  <h3>MailApp.sendEmail</h3>
  <div class="row-form">
    <input name="from" value="{{.Mail.From}}" placeholder="from address, e.g. workflows@example.com" size="48" />
  </div>
  <p class="note">The envelope sender for every sendEmail call. Bounces return here.</p>

  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save mail settings</button>
</form>

{{template "bottom.gohtml" .}}
